---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import RimeMark from "../components/RimeMark.astro";
import { MARK } from "../brand/mark";
const label = (k: string) => k.split("-").map((w) => w[0].toUpperCase() + w.slice(1)).join(" ");
const accents = Object.entries(MARK.accents);
const files = [
  ["rime-lockup-light.svg", "lockup, for light backgrounds"],
  ["rime-lockup-dark.svg", "lockup, for dark backgrounds"],
  ["rime-lockup-mono-black.svg", "lockup, one ink"],
  ["rime-lockup-mono-white.svg", "lockup, one ink"],
  ["rime-symbol-light.svg", "symbol, for light backgrounds"],
  ["rime-symbol-dark.svg", "symbol, for dark backgrounds"],
  ["rime-mark-black.svg", "symbol, one ink"],
  ["rime-mark-white.svg", "symbol, one ink"],
  ["rime-app-icon-dark-512.png", "app icon, 512 px"],
  ["rime-app-icon-light-512.png", "app icon, 512 px"],
];
---
<Base title="Brand" description="How to write Rime's name, how to use the layered ridge, and the one plane that takes a colour.">
  <header class="container page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Brand</p>
    <h1>Rime, and nothing more.</h1>
    <p class="lead">The name is Rime. "Rime OS" is for when you need to say the operating system specifically, and "Rime Shell" for the desktop. The website is rimeos.com.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="container section-tight brand-grid">
    <div class="mark-tile mark-dark"><RimeMark size={64} wordmark label="The Rime lockup on a dark background" /></div>
    <div class="mark-tile mark-light"><RimeMark size={64} wordmark label="The Rime lockup on a light background" /></div>
    <div class="mark-tile mark-mono"><RimeMark size={96} tone="mono" label="The Rime symbol in one ink" /></div>
    <div class="mark-tile mark-role"><RimeMark size={96} tone="role" label="The Rime symbol, its accent plane in this scene's colour" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section-tight prose">
    <h2>The layered ridge</h2>
    <p>The mark is four flat planes stacked into a rising ridge, with a lowercase <strong>rime</strong> beside it. The planes keep their shape and their order, bottom to peak, everywhere the mark appears. Below 32 pixels a version with slightly thinner planes keeps the gaps between them open.</p>
    <h2>Colour</h2>
    <p>Only the third plane ever takes a colour. It is Rime Blue unless something says otherwise; on Rime it follows the accent of your wallpaper, the way the rest of the desktop does. The other three planes and the word are the ink of whatever they sit on: dark on light, light on dark. Where only one colour is possible, all four planes take that colour.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container section-tight" aria-labelledby="accents-title">
    <h2 id="accents-title" class="visually-hidden">Accents</h2>
    <ul class="accent-row">
      {accents.map(([k, hex]) => (
        <li class="accent-tile">
          <RimeMark size={48} accent={hex} label={`The Rime symbol in ${label(k)}`} />
          <span class="caption">{label(k)}</span>
          <span class="caption mono">{hex.toUpperCase()}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="container section-tight prose prose-end">
    <h2>Writing the name</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Write <strong>Rime</strong>, with a capital R and nothing after it, in headlines and ordinary text. The lowercase <strong>rime</strong> belongs to the drawn mark only.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>Rime OS</strong> only when you need to name the operating system as distinct from the desktop, and <strong>Rime Shell</strong> for the desktop.</li>
      <li>Rime was called APEX-OS until 28 September 2026. Say so only where history or migration matters.</li>
      <li>The Rime input method for Chinese, packaged in Fedora as <code>ibus-rime</code>, is an unrelated project.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Files</h2>
    <ul>
      {files.map(([f, what]) => <li><a href={`/brand/${f}`} download>{f}</a> <span class="caption">{what}</span></li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .page-hero { padding-top: calc(var(--notch-h) + clamp(40px, 6vw, 88px)); padding-bottom: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px); display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .page-hero .lead { max-width: 60ch; }
  .brand-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .brand-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .mark-tile { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; border-radius: var(--radius-xl); display: grid; place-items: center; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rime-hairline); }
  /* The brand pack's own tiles and inks (rime-os files/branding/ridge/src/palette.json). */
  .mark-dark { background: #1f2327; color: #fafafa; }
  .mark-light { background: #fafafb; color: #212224; }
  .mark-mono { background: #fff; color: #000; }
  .mark-role { background: var(--rime-surface-raised); }
  .accent-row { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .accent-row { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .accent-tile { display: grid; justify-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 20px 8px 14px; border-radius: var(--radius-l); background: var(--rime-surface-raised); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rime-hairline); }
  .accent-tile :global(.rime-mark) { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .prose-end { padding-bottom: var(--section-pad); }
</style>
